   "evidence": "Glob of web/static_files/* lists no module-graph.*; pages.yml:143 \"versions tracked in web/static_files/ are just fallback snapshots\"; pages.yml:378 copies an asset only `if [ -s ... ]`.",
   "file": "web/Site/Theme.lean",
   "fix": "Commit a minimal `web/static_files/module-graph.html` placeholder (a page saying the graph is regenerated at deploy, matching the fallback-snapshot convention the other assets follow); the generated file overwrites it in the runner. Alternatively, drop the nav link until a fallback exists.",
   "issue": "`theme` adds `<a href=\"static/module-graph.html\">\"Modules\"</a>` to the nav on every page, but no `web/static_files/module-graph.html` exists in the repo. Every other site-referenced generated asset (loc-*.svg, participation.svg, progress.json, pr-stats.json) has a committed snapshot; pages.yml:142-145 states these tracked versions \"are just fallback snapshots so a local `cd web && lake exe web` renders something\". The link therefore 404s in any local build, and on a deploy where the new generation step fails before a first successful publish there is nothing to restore \u2014 pages.yml:378 (`if [ -s \"web/static_files/$asset\" ]`) silently skips a missing asset, so the broken nav entry ships without a CI failure.",
   "line": 32
  }
 ],
